  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="Tag1252" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;!--?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?--&gt;
&lt;div style="line-height: 108%; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;
&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Destin Pipeline Company, L.L.C.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Notes to Financial Statements&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Years Ended December 31, 2025 and 2024&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '1'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.49pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;1.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.49pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Organization and Nature of Business&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin Pipeline Company, L.L.C. ("Destin") was formed on February 28, 1997, under the provisions of the Delaware Limited Liability Company Act and as of December 31, 2018, its membership interests were 66.67% owned by Third Coast Emerald, L.L.C. ("Emerald") and 33.33% owned by Enbridge Offshore (Destin), L.L.C. ("Enbridge Destin").&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin was formed to construct, own and operate a 255-mile natural gas transport system with total capacity of 1.2 Bcf/d. The system originates offshore in the Gulf of Mexico and includes connections with four producing platforms and six producer-operated laterals. The 120-mile offshore portion of the Destin system terminates at the Pascagoula processing plant and is the single source of raw natural gas to the plant. The onshore portion of Destin is the sole delivery point for merchant-quality gas from the Pascagoula processing plant and extends 135 miles north in Mississippi. Destin currently serves as the primary transfer of gas flows from the Barnett and Haynesville Shale plays to Florida markets through interconnections with major interstate pipelines. Contracted volumes on the Destin pipeline are based on life-of-field dedication, dedicated volumes over a given period or interruptible volumes as capacity permits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin is engaged in interstate commerce and, as such, is subject to the rules, regulations and accounting procedures of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission, ("FERC") pursuant to the Natural Gas Act of 1938 and the Natural Gas Policy Act of 1978.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '2'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.49pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;2.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.49pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Summary of Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements prescribed by FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("GAAP").&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The most significant difference between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein is that FERC does not permit "push down" accounting for acquisitions.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Additionally, FERC requires that Destin reflect a hypothetical provision for federal and state income taxes and related balance sheet accounts, even though it is not subject to such taxes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with FERC regulations requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of certain assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the year. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Transportation and Exchange Gas Imbalances&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;In the course of providing transportation services, natural gas pipelines may receive different quantities of gas from shippers than the quantities delivered on behalf of those shippers.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;These transactions result in transportation and exchange gas imbalances.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Such shipper imbalances are recorded as Regulatory Assets or Regulatory Liabilities in the accompanying balance sheet using the posted index prices of the applicable approved tariffs, which approximate market rates.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;These imbalances are required to be resolved within a specified period of time or when certain quantity thresholds are met.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Resolution can be through imbalance trading with other shippers or by utilizing the cash out procedures specified in the tariff.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Exchange imbalances are settled with other pipelines through the cashout procedures in their tariffs and recorded to the income statement as Operating Expenses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Concentration of Credit Risk&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Accounts receivable are concentrated among shippers with operations in the Gulf of Mexico and in the state of Mississippi.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Concentrations of credit risk with respect to trade receivables are limited due to ongoing credit evaluations of customers.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin limits the amount of credit extended when deemed necessary and, generally, does not require collateral.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Concentrations of credit risk with respect to trade receivables are limited due to ongoing credit evaluations of customers.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;As of December 31, 2025, three customers had accounts receivable balances in excess of 10% of our accounts receivable, net, and represented approximately 87.23% of our outstanding accounts receivable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Significant customers are defined as those who represent 10% or more of the revenues during the year.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;For the year ended December 31, 2025, we had two customers which accounted for 43.71% of Destin's revenues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Allowance for Doubtful Accounts&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin establishes an allowance for losses on specific accounts receivable, as well as for gas imbalances due from shippers and operators, if collectability of such amounts is uncertain.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Collectability is reviewed periodically and the allowance is adjusted as necessary.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin had an allowance for doubtful accounts of $0 and $0 as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Cash and cash equivalents consist of cash balances and highly liquid investments that have an original maturity of three months or less when purchased.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;We place our cash and cash equivalents with high credit quality financial institutions. At times, our cash and cash equivalents may be uninsured or in deposit accounts that exceed the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation insurance limit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Pipelines and Equipment&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Pipelines and equipment, including transportation assets, are recorded at cost, less accumulated depreciation. Transportation assets consist primarily of line pipe, equipment, and other pipeline construction.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Additions and improvements that expand the productive capacity or extend the useful life of the System are capitalized.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Pipelines and equipment also include an Allowance for Funds Used during Construction (AFUDC). The rates used in the calculation of AFUDC are determined in accordance with guidelines established by the FERC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin determines depreciation using the straight-line method which allows Destin to effectively match depreciation expense with the expected utilization of the System. The pipeline and related facilities are depreciated at a straight-line rate of 5% per year.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Line fill, which is included in pipelines and equipment, represents natural gas acquired to commence operations of the pipeline and is valued at cost.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;See footnote 7 for details of Utility Plant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Impairment of Pipelines and Equipment&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin reviews pipelines and equipment assets for impairment whenever events or changes in circumstances indicate that the carrying amount of an asset may not be recoverable.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;When it becomes probable that all or a portion of any pipelines and equipment assets will be disallowed for rate-making purposes, such amounts are deducted from the reported cost of the asset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin is not subject to federal or state income taxes; however, the related tax impacts of its operations are reported on the tax returns of Destin&amp;#8217;s owners. For ratemaking purposes, Destin is treated as if it were a corporation that would require comprehensive income tax procedures.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;In accordance with FERC requirements, the accompanying financial statements include a hypothetical provision for federal and state income taxes as if Destin were a taxable entity following the guidance outlined in the Accounting Standards Codification 740, Income Taxes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Deferred tax assets and liabilities are recognized for the future tax consequences attributable to differences between the financial statement carrying amounts and the tax bases of existing assets and liabilities using enacted tax rates for the year in which the differences are expected to reverse.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;A valuation allowance is provided to offset deferred tax assets if, based upon the available evidence, it is more likely than not that some or all of the deferred tax assets will not be realized.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The current income tax provision for the year, which is reflected in Taxes Accrued on the balance sheet at year-end, will be relieved to Paid in Capital in the following year when the income tax returns are filed with the applicable tax authorities by Destin&amp;#8217;s members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;In 2014, the Financial Accounting Standards Board (&amp;#8220;FASB&amp;#8221;) issued Accounting Standards Update (&amp;#8220;ASU&amp;#8221;) No. 2014-09, &amp;#8220;Revenue from Contracts with Customers (Topic 606)&amp;#8221;, which supersedes most of the existing revenue recognition requirements in GAAP and requires entities to recognize revenue at an amount that reflects the consideration to which an entity expects to be entitled in exchange for transferring goods or services to a customer. It also requires significantly expanded disclosures regarding the qualitative and quantitative information of an entity&amp;#8217;s nature, amount, timing and uncertainty of revenue and cash flows arising from contracts with customers.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;We are not adopting the new standard for FERC reporting purposes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin follows Order No. 631, Accounting, Financial Reporting and Rate Filing Requirements for Asset Retirement Obligations ("ARO"), which addresses accounting and reporting for asset retirement obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived tangible assets.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Order No. 631 requires entities to record the fair value of a liability for the retirement obligation in the period in which the liability is incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The associated retirement cost is capitalized as part of the carrying value of the underlying asset, and is subsequently depreciated over the underlying asset's useful life.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;After initial recognition, the ARO is revised to reflect the passage of time through accretion and for changes in the estimate amount or timing of cash flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Legal obligations exist for certain of Destin's pipeline transmission assets as shown in Note 8. During 2025, the Company completed a new comprehensive abandonment study and has determined that its estimated abandonment liabilities have increased since its prior abandonment study completed in 2021, mainly due to changes in market rates for mobilization, flushing, cleaning, and other abandonment activities. As a result, for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2025 we recognized an upward revision of ARO in the amount of $0.6 million. There have been no other changes to the ARO as of December 31, 2025, and no abandonments in 2025 and 2024.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Financial Instruments&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Destin&amp;#8217;s financial instruments consist of cash, accounts receivable and accounts payable.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The carrying amount of these financial instruments represents their fair value based on their short-term nature.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '3'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.49pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;3.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.49pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Related-Party Transactions&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Transportation Services&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;During 2025 and 2024, no transportation revenues were earned from related parties. All transportation revenues earned were at rates pursuant to the existing tariffs.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Operating and Administrative Expenses&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Since Destin has no employees, operating, maintenance, and general and administrative services are provided under service agreements with the operator.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Substantially all labor costs, audit, insurance and management fees operating/ administrative expenses were incurred through services provided under these agreements during 2025 and 2024 for $6,496,112 and $7,109,724, respectively.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;On December 31, 2025 and 2024, Destin had affiliate payables of $647,064 and $1,570,044, respectively, relating to these agreements.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '4'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.49pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;4.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.49pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Regulatory Assets and Liabilities&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Regulatory Assets and Regulatory Liabilities include shipper imbalances, lost and unaccounted for gas ("LAUF"), Allowance for Funds Under Construction (&amp;#8220;AFUDC&amp;#8221;), Annual Charge Assessments (&amp;#8220;ACA&amp;#8221;) and adjustments for excess/grossed-up deferred income taxes.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;On December 31, 2025 and 2024, Regulatory Assets totaled &lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;$352,022 and $309,126, respectively.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;At December 31, 2025 and 2024, Regulatory Liabilities totaled $13,222,196 and $13,391,517, respectively.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '5'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.49pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;5.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.49pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Deferred income taxes are provided for temporary differences between the tax basis of Destin's assets and liabilities and the amounts reported in the financial statements.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The changes in the net deferred tax accounts for the years ending December 31, 2025 and 2024, were as follows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
